{"title":"PaperMath’s sum","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>PaperMath's sum is a thereom discovered by the AoPS user Papermath on October 8th, 2023.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>PaperMath’s sum</b> states,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2caa93db21887310124c7d1d6162baea53f4cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{2n-1} {\\left(10^ix^2\\right)}=\\left(\\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}{\\left(10^j3x\\right)}\\right)^2 + \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} {\\left(10^k2x^2\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"364\" height=\"61\" />\n</p><p>Or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8713ac266f3d8ebb0ee2e9d91825e607e45730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\sum_{i=0}^{2n-1} {10^i}=\\left(3x \\sum_{j=0}^{n-1} {\\left(10^j\\right)}\\right)^2 + 2x^2\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} {\\left(10^k\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"357\" height=\"61\" />\n</p><p>For all real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, this equation holds true for all nonnegative values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, this reduces to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/159de51eea1913f25984e8bfe69d2ccc2bb88dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{2n-1} {10^i}=\\left(\\sum_{j=0}^{n -1}{\\left(3 \\times 10^j\\right)}\\right)^2 + \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} {\\left(2 \\times 10^k\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"347\" height=\"61\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> part is trivial multiplication, associativity, commutativity, and distributivity over addition,\n</p><p>Observing that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82ef2cd5f85e071112cb2e0723c7cddc16430247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=0}^{n-1} {10^i} = \\frac{10^{n}-1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"55\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8559658f077fef418b12c4ed83565381b47073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10^{2n}-1)/9 = 9((10^{n}-1)/9)^2 + 2(10^n -1)/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"367\" height=\"21\" /> concludes the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and nonzero digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />; let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9be2b1de79fff66db67de3b18303bdd2912b7ae6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e173907ca992482385a50c6f62ede920362b1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />-digit (not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit) integer each of whose digits is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. What is the greatest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> for which there are at least two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee2898536ac76874d818128c0569ec0144a18356.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n - B_n = A_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"19\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bbdd14d411a771654ba58aa06462df94668ae4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 16 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 18 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">Source</a>)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_sum\" title=\"Cyclic sum\">Cyclic sum</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Summation\" title=\"Summation\">Summation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetric_sum\" title=\"Symmetric sum\">Symmetric sum</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=PaperMath%E2%80%99s_sum&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234807\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 154/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 304/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5199/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.913      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.913      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25427:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234807 and revision id 263993. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}